    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** (79.31) and **Bryce Harper** (75.38) anchor our lineup as the premier offensive threats. **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against J. Lopez, where a favorable park environment and a significant SP skill edge boost his efficiency score well into the elite tier. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** draws a prime opportunity against G. Holmes; his score is driven by a +17% SP skill advantage and a top-tier lineup spot, making him the most reliable cornerstone for our Roto categories today. We are also looking for significant output from **Lawrence Butler** (72.24), who is riding a dual-threat wave of a +10% park factor and a BvP historical edge that makes him one of our most dangerous options against B. Miller.\n\nThe margin between our starters and the bench remains razor-thin, as evidenced by the case of **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.39). While **Jung Hoo Lee** earned a boost from wind conditions, the combination of a difficult matchup against N. Pivetta and superior projected efficiency from the likes of **Zack Gelof**\u2014whose score is propped up by an elite BvP history and a delivery speed factor that favors his stolen base potential\u2014ultimately kept him on the pine. We are monitoring the situation closely, as **Masyn Winn** and **Alex Freeland** sit in the marginal category (sub-50); if we need to chase efficiency late in the day, we are prepared to pivot to our bench depth. While no specific weather hazards are currently flagged, the overall SP environment is relatively soft across our primary bats, leaving us well-positioned to maintain our lead in AVG and power-based categories.",
